From 4300e6b45268ed4adbf992ab2e58445f9d0eb7ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:43:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vr: expose Steam Frame controllers to WebXR

Add the /interaction_profiles/valve/frame_controller_valve OpenXR
interaction profile from XR_VALVE_frame_controller_interaction, reported
to pages as "valve-frame" with a "generic-trigger-squeeze-thumbstick"
fallback. Component paths follow Valve's published profile
(ValveSoftware/Unity, SteamFrameControllerProfile.cs).

The Frame splits a full gamepad across two controllers: A/B/X/Y and a
menu button on the right, a D-pad and a view button on the left, and a
shoulder button, grip, trigger and thumbstick on both. Without the
profile SteamVR presents the controllers as emulated Touch controllers,
so the D-pad, shoulder buttons and view are lost.

Gamepad layout (xr-standard, then fixed Frame slots so the indices do
not shift when a component is unbound):
  0 trigger, 1 squeeze, 2 touchpad placeholder, 3 thumbstick
  right: 4 A, 5 B, 6 X, 7 Y, 8 shoulder, 9 menu
  left:  4 D-pad up, 5 down, 6 left, 7 right, 8 shoulder, 9 view

The Frame menu button gets its own button type (kAppMenu) instead of
kMenu, which OpenXRInputHelper treats as the exit gesture; on the Frame
the system button and SteamVR dashboard already end a session.

Suggesting bindings stays fatal for every other profile, but a rejected
Frame suggestion is skipped so input keeps working through the
runtime's remapping.

Bug: none
Test: device_unittests --gtest_filter='OpenXrInteractionProfilesTest.*'
